  "known_external_failure": "Unchanged P0a test-design-checks sandbox lacks apps/center/src/app.ts, as on qualified main; recorded as exit 1, not a pass.",
  "known_limits": [
    "SIGKILL of the wrapper itself leaves the postmaster, socket directory and data root behind (B, unchanged).",
    "A command descendant that deliberately leaves its process group survives (B, unchanged).",
    "EPERM for a live command group is not reachable as this user; stop-failure reporting is proved with an injected fault in a disposable source copy (mock, named).",
    "A never-ready live server is produced with a pg_isready shim that always exits 1; the server, roles and cleanup are real.",
    "On macOS a SIGKILLed postmaster leaves its 56-byte System V shared memory interlock segment; kern.sysv.shmmni=32 caps the number of clusters that can start until unattached segments with dead creators are removed with ipcrm. Found during C when 31 orphans from earlier lanes blocked initdb; sysv-shm-sweep.json records the one-time removal.",
    "A same-user listener bound at the exact dead postmaster socket path with the lock untouched is unlinked as the stale socket (foreign-listener-exact-lock); same-user hostile code is outside the accepted boundary and the model was not broadened.",
    "A SIGINT that lands while initdb is running its bootstrap backend leaves that backend's System V segment on macOS; the wrapper never saw a postmaster, so its run-owned reclaim cannot name it. The scenario driver records such segments under environment_diff.segments.added and exact-head/sysv-shm-own-segments.json removes only those, after proving the creator dead and the segment unattached. Found by sigint-sweep during the reconciliation rerun; the wrapper is unchanged."
  ],
